#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""LU-POI TRADER v14 - single-file live MT5 bot for XAUUSD.t.

This is the complete v14, built as ONE python file.  It is the package version
(trader.py + the lubot package + the two helpers from bot.py) inlined in
dependency order, byte-for-byte in behaviour.  It contains the live trader, the
v14 martingale sizing and the M1 portfolio simulator, so it can live-trade and
backtest:

    python lubot_trader_v14_single.py --backtest --csv data/xauusd_m1.csv

Live trading:
    python lubot_trader_v14_single.py --symbol XAUUSD.t --risk 1.0 --min-quality 0.50 \\
        --commission 7 --timeframes M5,M10,M15,M30,H1 \\
        --trader "tp_levels=0.6|1.2|2.4|4.8,tp_fracs=1|1|1|1,ladder_fallback=merge,\\
dedupe_cross_tf=false,keep_replaced_bars=1,keep_replaced_tfs=M10|M15|M30|H1,\\
regime_metric=adr_ratio,regime_threshold=1.0,regime_short=5,regime_long=20,\\
range_tp_levels=0.5|1.0|1.5|2.5,range_tp_fracs=1|1|1|1,range_sl_after_leg=0|0.3|x|x,\\
mart_mode=mult,mart_mult=1.5,mart_max_steps=3,mart_max_risk_pct=3,mart_scope=tf,\\
mart_tfs=M10|M15|M30|H1,mart_sides=buy,mart_ungated_scale=0.5" \\
        --trade-filter "M5:max_cost_r=0.08;min_quality=0.55;sessions=asia|london|preny|ny|lclose/M10:min_quality=0.57/M15:min_quality=0.60/M30|H1:min_quality=0.57" \\
        --confluence-filter "M5:max_cost_r=0.08;min_quality=0.55;sessions=asia|london|preny|ny|lclose/M10:min_quality=0.50/M15:min_quality=0.60/M30|H1:min_quality=0.57" \\
        --state trader_state.json --log trader.log

NO login option: the bot attaches to the MetaTrader 5 terminal that is already
open and logged in on this Windows PC.  ``pip install MetaTrader5`` and keep the
terminal running.  THIS BUILD IS COMPLETE: the v14-A data is embedded, so nothing has to sit
alongside it.  The quality model (models/quality_model.json) and the recorded full-year selection
stream (study_results/sel_v10_<TF>.pkl) are stored inside this file and written to disk on first use
when absent; the backtest below therefore reproduces the v14-A study from the CSV alone.

    models/quality_model.json          (embedded; override with --set quality_model_path=...)

v14-A (study_results/MARTINGALE_V14.md) = v13-A + the ASYMMETRIC, edge-aware
MARTINGALE: after a losing plan a per-timeframe streak steps the NEXT plans of the
SAME timeframe - M10/M15/M30/H1 BUY plans x1.5 UP (max 3 steps, max 3 % of equity),
every other plan (M5, sells) x0.5 DOWN; a win resets the streak, break-even exits are
neutral.  The streak is rebuilt from trader_state.json on every start (a restart
cannot lose or double a streak).  v13-A (study_results/WEAK_MONTHS_V13.md) remains the
base: regime_metric=adr_ratio < 1.0 -> tight ladder + break-even/+0.3R range
management.  Account protection: daily loss 4.5 % -> flat until the next server day,
total loss 9 % -> HALT (--max-daily-loss / --max-total-loss, 0 = off).  Hedging account
required for the ladder (netting -> two-leg fallback).  All risk constraints (risk_pct,
martingale caps, daily/total loss limits, max_pending_orders, broker stop distance,
margin buffer) are enforced in the code below.
"""
from __future__ import annotations


import argparse
import glob
import io
import json
import logging
import math
import os
import sys
import time
from dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field, fields
from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Tuple
from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

